<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōtomo clan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Otomo clan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ōtomo clan was a Japanese warrior family that held Bungo province in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> as military governors from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> period. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otomo-sorin">Ōtomo Sōrin</a>, who became a Christian, it dominated northern Kyushu in the mid-16th century, but it was crushed by the Shimazu at Mimikawa in 1578. It survived under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> until he confiscated Bungo in 1593.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otomo-clan.jpg" alt="Ōtomo clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Daki_hana_Gyouyou.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
